Example recordings in samples/
------------------------------
Every file under samples/ is a short excerpt from a publicly published EEG
dataset, cropped and rewritten as EDF so the website can offer something to try
without hosting whole studies. samples/manifest.json records, for each file,
which source file it came from and which seconds were taken.

Sources and licences:

  EEG dataset of consumer- and research-grade systems
  Ahn, M. and Lee, Y. (2026). Figshare. CC BY 4.0
  https://doi.org/10.6084/m9.figshare.30162868

  OpenNeuro ds002718, from Wakeman, D. G. and Henson, R. N. (2015),
  "A multi-subject, multi-modal human neuroimaging dataset". CC0
  https://openneuro.org/datasets/ds002718

  iNCog-EEG. Figshare. CC BY 4.0
  https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/iNCog-EEG_ideal_vs_Noisy_Cognitive_EEG_for_Workload_Assessment_Dataset/30003127

Only these excerpts are redistributed. The full datasets are not hosted here.
Please cite the groups above rather than this site if you use the data.
